      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-167888",
      ":question/problem": "A heating element $E$ lies on the intersection of the cylindrical heater and the plane $z=2.$ Use your answer to part 4 to find an outward-pointing unit normal vector $n(x,y)$ to $E$ that lies within this plane. Express your answer in terms of $x$ and $y.$\n\n*Hint: The matrix ${R}_{z}(\u03d5)$ representing a counterclockwise rotation of $\u03d5$ radians about the $z$-axis is given by*\n\n$$\n{R}_{z}(\u03d5)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5 & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5 & 0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5 & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $n(x,y)=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,i+\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                   